CWPP MUSIC PROMPT — “KALEIDOSCOPE GIRL”
CORE INTENT (LOCKED)

Summon a late-1967 psychedelic pop dreamscape with surreal imagery, childlike wonder, and drifting consciousness — whimsical on the surface, quietly uncanny underneath.

TEMPO & GROOVE (HIGH WEIGHT)
Slow–moderate tempo: ~95–105 BPM
Loose 4/4, gently floating, never driving
Groove feels suspended, like walking on soft ground
Drums are felt, not foregrounded — light kick, brushed/snapped snare, soft tambourine accents

HARMONIC LANGUAGE (VERY HIGH WEIGHT)
Dreamy major-key center with frequent non-functional shifts
Chords feel like they slide sideways rather than resolve
Use:
modal color (Mixolydian / Lydian flavor)
unexpected chord lifts under static melody notes
Harmony should feel storybook-surreal, not blues-based

MELODY & VOCALS (CRITICAL)
Lead vocal: male, light, slightly nasal, intimate
Melody is simple, chant-like, narrow range
Phrasing feels childlike, observational, almost narrated
Backing vocals:
airy “ahh” / “ooh” stacks
float above and behind the lead
feel like characters in a dream replying

INSTRUMENTATION (IDENTITY LOCK)
Low-register organ (reedy, almost fairground-like)
Electric piano / celeste tones for sparkle
Gentle acoustic guitar strums, minimal attack
Bass: rounded, melodic, drifting rather than grooving
Occasional psychedelic ornamentation:
reversed swells
tape flutter
light phasing

⚠️ No heavy distortion.
⚠️ No blues-rock aggression.
⚠️ No modern synths.

ARRANGEMENT SHAPE (PROCEDURAL)
Opening: instantly surreal — no long intro
organ establishes dream-world in first second
Verse sections: sparse, narrative, observational
Refrain: harmony blooms, backing vocals widen stereo field
Bridge: brief harmonic left-turn — curious, not dramatic
Return: familiar but slightly more saturated
Outro: fades like waking up mid-thought

PRODUCTION & TEXTURE (LOCKED)
1967 analog warmth
Slight tape wobble, mono-leaning center with soft stereo bleed
Reverb is plate-like, short tails, not cavernous
Everything feels close but unreal

LYRICAL GUIDANCE (ABSTRACTED – SAFE)
Use nonsense-surreal imagery:
colors behaving like objects
animals doing human things
landscapes made of improbable materials
perspective shifts (above / below / inside)

👉 Tone: gentle wonder, not irony
👉 Mood: dream logic, not metaphor explanation

NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS (ENFORCED)
❌ No modern pop polish
❌ No trap / EDM rhythm
❌ No blues pentatonic leads
❌ No epic build or drop

TARGET EFFECT (THE TEST)
If someone hears this and says:
“This feels like a children’s book written on acid in 1967”
you hit it.